Z||000016||Gerald||12-05-2001||12:19 AM||||I raced a guy in a 87 gt 5spd with my 87 base coupe. He won but still didnt belive I had the duke in it till I showed him. Rolling start from 70 kph. We were on it hard all the way to 160 kph. My car is falling to pieces now but I cant affored to fix it till jan. Still no one laughs at it.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Fierobsessed||12-05-2001||02:43 AM||||I welcome that first impression, my decklid says 2m4, I have single exhaust, 13" skinny alloys from an oldsmobile, and there is a nice hole where the trunk lock used to be. it looks pretty slow. It has a 3.1 DIS V6, the only way you can tell its not a 4 is the loud growl sound, and it eats rice.||||reg||12
Z||000018||Fformula88||12-05-2001||10:17 AM||||I have rarely had people "laugh" because I had a four.  I get more people who do not have a clue as to what is in it ask me, either because they have long since forgotten or never knew what engines were available.<P>Before I got the wing back on, I had a few suckers try me from stop lights and such with Saturns and other 4-bangers, but since I got the wing painted and back on that hasn't been much of a problem.<P>My biggest nussance is Celcia GTS owners... they always want to race but only when they are already moving.  If a stop light turns red, they find a reason to turn or otherwise not be at the line with me.  At least they know they have no torque!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">    <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000019||Kelvin Vivian||12-05-2001||09:22 PM||||I have an 87 SE that I love, 87 SEs are "aero-notchbacks" exactly like 85 GTs, Indy Fieros, and the 86 SE.<P>As can be seen from someone approaching the car, the car includes from the factory: spoiler, sunroof, and dual twin-pipe exhausts.<P>Non-factory items I've added are: 15-in GT grey rims, and a holley side-scoop.<P>BUT, the SE is a 4-cyl, so I get the opposite reaction, most think I have a V6, when I have the 4-cyl.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>The 4-cyl does pack quite a punch.  Plus I average around 35 miles/gallon.<P>KV<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.printroom.com/_vti_bin/ViewImage.dll?userid=no_18&album_id=36084&image_id=3&courtesy=1">    <BR>88 GT, 5-spd<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||14
